course: dictionary
lesson: 9080
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Sloth has two: an animal, and laziness. Context tells you which one the writer means. Read the words around it and ask: is this about a creature, or about not wanting to work?
explain: «Imagine being so slow that green algae grow in your hair and moths live in it.» Here sloth is an animal, because the sentence is about fur, leaves and trees. In «as slow as a sloth» it is the animal too, and it shows how slow something moves.
explain: Sloth also means laziness, but this is a formal or old word, so you will mostly meet it in books and older stories. Check the sentence: if it talks about a creature, use the animal meaning; if it talks about not wanting to do work, use laziness.
fact: A sloth is a slow-moving animal from Central and South America.
fact: Sloths hang upside down in trees and sleep many hours a day.
fact: Green algae can grow in a sloth's fur and help to hide it among the leaves.
fact: A two-toed sloth has two claws on each front foot and three on each back foot.
fact: Sloth also means laziness, and it is a formal or old word.
exercise: «A two-toed sloth has two claws on each front foot.» In this sentence, what is a sloth? | A type of cloud | A river in South America | A kind of tree | *An animal
exercise: «He spent the whole day in sloth, refusing to lift a finger.» What does sloth mean here? | A slow-moving animal in the trees | A kind of food | *Laziness | A river crossing
exercise: «Her slowness was as slow as a sloth.» In the phrase «as slow as a sloth», what is the sloth used to show? | How happy someone feels | How big something is | *How very slow something is | How hungry someone is
test: «In the cartoon «Ice Age» a mammoth, a sabre-toothed cat and a ground sloth travel together.» Is the ground sloth an animal or laziness here? | A kind of tree | Laziness | *An animal
test: Which meaning fits best in «The old king's sloth made the kingdom poor»? | A slow-moving animal | A cave | A river | *Laziness
exam: «Green algae grow in a sloth's fur and help to hide it among the leaves.» Why does the algae help the sloth? | To help it climb faster | *To help hide it among the leaves | To warm its toes | To make it lazy
